#
# Code owners for AI_LM. GitHub requests a review from the matching owner
# whenever a pull request touches one of these paths.
#
# !! PLACEHOLDER TEAMS !!
# The handles below do NOT exist yet. Before opening this repository to outside
# contributors a maintainer must:
#   1. Create the teams under the @FutureBuildAIinc organisation
#      (Settings -> Teams). Suggested: maintainers, backend, frontend, infra,
#      legal — or collapse them all to `maintainers` if the split is premature.
#   2. Give each team at least *write* access to this repository. GitHub
#      silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries for teams without write access, so a
#      typo or a missing grant looks exactly like "nothing happened".
#   3. Replace every handle here with the real one.
#   4. Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection rule
#      for `main`, alongside the required "CI" status check.
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins, so the specific overrides at the bottom
# take precedence over the catch-all at the top.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner for everything not matched below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                           @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/backend/                   @FutureBuildAIinc/backend
/app/                       @FutureBuildAIinc/frontend

# The GableLBM integration client is the entire dependency surface between
# AI_LM and the ERP. A change here changes the contract, not just the code.
/backend/internal/gable/    @FutureBuildAIinc/backend @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# Axle, GVW, volume, and securement math. A wrong answer in these files is a
# safety and legal exposure for the dealer running the truck, not a display
# bug — they get maintainer eyes regardless of how small the diff looks.
/backend/internal/load/     @FutureBuildAIinc/backend @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/backend/internal/compliance/ @FutureBuildAIinc/backend @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# Database migrations are append-only and irreversible in production.
/backend/migrations/        @FutureBuildAIinc/backend @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI, deploy, and container plumbing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                   @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/.do/                       @FutureBuildAIinc/infra @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/docker-compose.yml         @FutureBuildAIinc/infra
/backend/Dockerfile         @FutureBuildAIinc/infra
/app/Dockerfile             @FutureBuildAIinc/infra
/app/nginx.conf.template    @FutureBuildAIinc/infra

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensing, legal, and policy — maintainer approval always required. These
# files define what the project *is* legally; a bad merge here is far more
# expensive to unwind than a bad merge in application code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/LICENSE                    @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/LICENSE-MAP.md             @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/LICENSES/                  @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/REUSE.toml                 @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/SECURITY.md                @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md         @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
